course: dictionary
lesson: 1724
title: Citric acid and sour taste
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from a word you may already know. Citric comes from citrus, the group of fruits that includes lemons, limes and oranges. «That sharp, sour taste is the taste of an acid: lemons are full of citric acid.» The words around citric, lemons and acid, give you the clue.
explain: Citric acid is a weak acid found in citrus fruits, and it is why they taste sour. «Sour tastes come from acids; lemons contain citric acid, and sour sweets are dusted with acid powder that stings the tongue.» The sentence shows that sour sweets can also contain acid.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «lemons are full of citrus acid»: it still makes sense, so citric means to do with citrus fruits. Good scientists check their words this way too.
fact: Citric means to do with, or coming from, citrus fruits such as lemons, limes and oranges.
fact: Citric acid is a weak acid that gives citrus fruits their sour taste.
fact: In a science lesson, lemon juice turns blue litmus paper red, which shows it is an acid.
fact: Citric acid mixed with baking soda fizzes, as it does in sherbet and bath bombs.
fact: In food, citric acid (E330) is added to sweets and drinks for a sour taste and to help keep food fresh.
exercise: What does citric mean? | *To do with citrus fruits such as lemons | To do with sleeping at night | To do with metal and iron | To do with cold weather
exercise: «Lemons are full of citric acid.» Which substance gives lemons their sour taste? | *Citric acid | Water | Sugar | Baking soda
exercise: In science, what happens when citric acid is mixed with baking soda? | It makes a loud bang | It freezes solid | It turns blue | *It fizzes
test: Why is citric acid (E330) added to sweets and drinks? | *To give a sour taste and help keep food fresh | To make them heavier | To turn them blue | To make them colder
test: What colour does lemon juice turn blue litmus paper? | Black | Yellow | *Red | Green
exam: Citric acid is found in which fruits? | *Lemons and limes | Apples and pears | Potatoes and carrots | Bananas and grapes
